    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d472">

                <pb facs="0437" n="427" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg427"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">394.1115/74: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-09-01">September 1,
                        1941</date>.<lb/>[Received September 1—2:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1194. Fifty-nine Americans reached Shanghai August 30th aboard <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Tatuta Maru</hi>, including 10 Foreign Service
                    personnel, 9 Army officers, 4 Navy officers, 1 Navy wife and 1 Navy child.</p>
                <p>Huffman and Smith sailed <hi rendition="#italic">Garfield</hi> today for
                    Bombay.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
